                    <occupation>Clerk</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Ed Pope noes: Letter 1.7.1807 to Godwin, Bodleian Abinger c.10 f.43 from
                            M C Springsguth late clerk to Mr Nicholson at Mr Withers, Palsgrave
                            Place, Temple Bar. He was in custody there having given security for
                            Nicholson (William DNB 1753-1815) in the presence of Fletcher and Heath,
                            "Sloper knows and has done nothing". Matthew Clix Springsguth bapt
                            10.6.1777 Covent Garden of Samuel and Ann, bur 20.5.1824 St Clement Danes
                            age 45 of Shire Lane> His father Joachim Samuel Springsguth habit maker
                            will PCC 22.4.1795, mother Ann will PCC 5.5.1812. Matthew Clix
                            Springsguth bach otp = Soho 23.10.1832 Frances Ann Few sp otp by lic
                            sigs wits Charles Robertson, Isabel Greig </p>
                    </note>
